-// amx_fused_bench.cpp — fused-page software-attention benchmark.
-//
-// Self-contained (no tron includes; compiles with plain g++), but uses the
-// EXACT tron kv_block layouts so numbers transfer:
-//   K page: [64 tokens][128 dims] bf16 row-major, row stride 256 B
-//   V page: [32 pairs][128 dims][2] bf16 token-pair-interleaved (AMX B format)
-// and replicates the shipping kernels' instruction patterns for the AVX
-// baseline (dotter: 4x vdpbf16ps + hreduce per (token, query);
-// scaled_v: 8 fp32 accumulators, vdpbf16ps over pair-interleaved V).
-//
-// The canonical-K AMX formulation (see Note [Mirror orientation] in
-// h/tron/kernels/amx_attn_iface.hpp):
-//   QK:  S^T[64 x Nq] = K_page[64x128] . Q_pack^T   (K consumed AS STORED)
-//   PV:  O[Nq x 128] += P[Nq x 64] . V_page          (V consumed AS STORED)
-// Fused per page: QK tiles -> store S^T -> transpose(+scale) -> running max
-// -> exp -> P pack (bf16) -> PV tiles -> store O -> v* rescale/add.
-//
-// Tile policy: ONE max-shape LDTILECFG per bench region (all tiles 16x64B);
-// query width is handled by zero-padding Q columns / P rows (a padded lane
-// costs nothing extra in the fixed TDP slot). TILERELEASE on exit.
-//
-// Variants:
-//   avx     : dotter-pattern QK + shared softmax + scaled_v-pattern PV
-//   amx44   : our fused AMX path, PV output blocking 4+4
-//   amx62   : our fused AMX path, PV output blocking 6+2
-// Usage: amx_fused_bench [Nq] [iters] [variant] [pages]
-//   pages = ring size for residency control (1 = L2-resident page,
-//           512 = ~16 MB > L2, 32768 = ~1 GB > LLC slice share)
-//
-// Correctness: every variant is checked against a scalar reference once
-// (rel tol 2e-2, matching t_amx_attention practice) before timing.
